# allgather_test.cm
#
# In-network AllGather over a 4-member group (one host per pod on a
# 16-host K=4 fat tree, so each member sits under a distinct ToR).
#
# The gathered vector is 16384 bytes = 4 equal blocks of 4096 bytes. Member i
# contributes block i and multicasts it into the group:
#
#   host 0  -> block 0,  host 4  -> block 1,
#   host 8  -> block 2,  host 12 -> block 3
#
# All |G| sources inject concurrently under one shared group_id + op_flow_id.
# handle_mcast RPF-fans each member's block to every member except itself, so
# each member receives the |G|-1 = 3 OTHER blocks over the fabric (its own
# block stays local). Each member ends holding all 4 blocks. Completion
# (ALLGATHER_COMPLETE) fires once all 4 members have received 3*4096 = 12288
# bytes. AllGather is the dual of Reduce-Scatter.
#
# Requires: size divisible by |G| (16384 / 4 = 4096) and the resulting block
# size (4096) a multiple of the MTU (2048 or 4096) so the per-sink byte-count
# completion is exact.
Nodes 16
Grp 0 4 8 12
Connections 1
0->0 id 1 start_allgather 0 size 16384
